            {
                "entry_id": "ee11d046-80a7-31f7-95e9-8dbdf78fb742",
                "word": "spoonerism",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "58dafddf-ee22-4d1c-93f7-1c76ed8047f5",
                        "entry_id": "ee11d046-80a7-31f7-95e9-8dbdf78fb742",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "spoonerisms"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6d996791-d1a0-3c9e-894c-cd3d52d994c5",
                        "entry_id": "ee11d046-80a7-31f7-95e9-8dbdf78fb742",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A play on words on a phrase in which the initial (usually consonantal) sounds of two or more of the main words are transposed."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "30cd43c4-e6d6-4e9a-aaf1-27b76e334bed",
                                "sense_id": "6d996791-d1a0-3c9e-894c-cd3d52d994c5",
                                "text": "Undergraduates at Oxford University were playfully fond of Spooner, whom they nicknamed \"the Spoo\". They also coined the term \"spoonerism\" around 1885, after Spooner had been a fellow at New College for almost twenty years. By 1892, his reputation for absentmindedness was well known; students came to New College expecting to hear a spoonerism."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e7a1007d-b11a-49ab-bea4-004de00b5160",
                        "source_entry_id": "ee11d046-80a7-31f7-95e9-8dbdf78fb742",
                        "source_sense_id": "6d996791-d1a0-3c9e-894c-cd3d52d994c5",
                        "source_sense_description": "phrase where sounds are transposed",
                        "target_lang_word": "spoonerisme",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "spoonerisme",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "000dbf38-2b18-3f63-a000-eecb04f151a7",
                                        "entry_id": "c8be9cb6-d7f8-3ee2-828d-4b2a2e76afd1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "verspreking door verwisseling van klanken van verschillende woorden"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99d8a10e-5314-4a02-81d5-680f118a366e",
                                                "sense_id": "000dbf38-2b18-3f63-a000-eecb04f151a7",
                                                "text": "Een spoonerisme is bijvoorbeeld: \"zeetakje\" inplaats van \"theezakje\" of \"met verkrachte eenden\" inplaats van \"met vereende krachten\"."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6548c708-a5f1-439d-b0d6-f5441fd9e632",
                        "source_entry_id": "ee11d046-80a7-31f7-95e9-8dbdf78fb742",
                        "source_sense_id": "6d996791-d1a0-3c9e-894c-cd3d52d994c5",
                        "source_sense_description": "phrase where sounds are transposed",
                        "target_lang_word": "contrepèterie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "contrepèterie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "59eee16d-4637-3505-9597-d3283b0932d8",
                                        "entry_id": "3957e982-0338-3a01-a83b-d67c3510e9b9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Jeu de mots consistant à permuter des lettres, des syllabes, ou des phonèmes dans un énoncé pour en créer un autre plus comique (généralement grivois ou irrévérencieux)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e6f2155-87b9-40d5-9e5a-205e71b93892",
                                                "sense_id": "59eee16d-4637-3505-9597-d3283b0932d8",
                                                "text": "La « femme folle de la messe » transformé par Rabelais en « femme molle de la fesse » est le prototype de la contrepèterie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26cd2129-3bb8-4d0c-98c8-1595f9d69d4a",
                                                "sense_id": "59eee16d-4637-3505-9597-d3283b0932d8",
                                                "text": "Le Canard enchainé est célèbre pour sa rubrique hebdomadaire de contrepèteries intitulée Sur l’album de la Comtesse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7406744a-6484-495b-a1f5-1ca70b136dd5",
                                                "sense_id": "59eee16d-4637-3505-9597-d3283b0932d8",
                                                "text": "Avec l’expression « femme déçue », on peut faire la contrepèterie « dame fessue »."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bc27165-c069-4a15-b873-d27928e0f1b4",
                                                "sense_id": "59eee16d-4637-3505-9597-d3283b0932d8",
                                                "text": "« Bicyclette » a pour contrepèterie « cybiclette »."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83a9ee4d-d6d9-42b9-ad9e-b748275d25b8",
                                                "sense_id": "59eee16d-4637-3505-9597-d3283b0932d8",
                                                "text": "Contrairement à son habitude, Marc ne plaisanta pas, ne fit pas de mauvais jeu de mots, ne déguisa pas sa voix, ne commença pas la conversation par une contrepèterie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e950bfd6-b321-4255-bac9-debc81f0acaf",
                                                "sense_id": "59eee16d-4637-3505-9597-d3283b0932d8",
                                                "text": "Quant aux esprits chagrins, nous nous bornons à les renvoyer à cette contrepèterie belge qui les rassurera : « Il fait beau et chaud… »"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fc266d77-3327-415a-b95e-015e6b6ad9d2",
                        "source_entry_id": "ee11d046-80a7-31f7-95e9-8dbdf78fb742",
                        "source_sense_id": "6d996791-d1a0-3c9e-894c-cd3d52d994c5",
